WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.895 --> 00:00:18.916
15 Dear Daddy Longlegs, It's very stormy outside tonight.

2
00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:23.017
All the girls have turned off their lights and gone to sleep.

3
00:00:24.478 --> 00:00:27.319
But I drank black coffee, so I can't sleep.

4
00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:32.400
I had a party in my room this evening for Sallie and Julia.

5
00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:37.034
We ate sardines, muffins, salad, and fudge.

6
00:00:41.818 --> 00:00:44.679
We also drank coffee, which I'm now regretting!

7
00:00:44.699 --> 00:00:50.103
"I had fun," Julia said as she was leaving.

8
00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.044
Imagine that!

9
00:00:52.705 --> 00:00:55.467
An orphan successfully entertained a Pendleton.

10
00:00:57.448 --> 00:00:58.809
But Sallie was the true friend.

11
00:01:01.531 --> 00:01:03.012
She stayed and helped with the dishes.

12
00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.341
Would you mind pretending that you're my grandmother?

13
00:01:08.682 --> 00:01:10.283
I know that's a strange request!

14
00:01:12.184 --> 00:01:14.806
But tonight the other girls were comparing their grandmothers.

15
00:01:14.826 --> 00:01:18.708
"I have one grandmother," Sallie said.

16
00:01:18.728 --> 00:01:20.689
"She's lots of fun."

17
00:01:20.709 --> 00:01:24.551
"I have two grandmothers," Julia said.

18
00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:29.774
Well, of course, she has more grandmothers than anyone does!

19
00:01:29.794 --> 00:01:33.256
A grandmother seems like a nice relative to have.

20
00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:40.837
When I went into town yesterday, I saw a lace cap trimmed with lilac ribbon.

21
00:01:42.418 --> 00:01:43.138
Would you like that?

22
00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:46.999
I'll buy it for your 83rd birthday, Granny dear.

23
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:55.982
Meanwhile I am studying verb forms for my Latin exam.

24
00:01:56.002 --> 00:01:58.683
I have studied verb forms for my exam.

25
00:02:00.223 --> 00:02:03.124
I will be studying verb forms for my exam.

26
00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:08.626
The exam is next week, and I have vowed to pass it!

27
00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.968
The clock in the chapel is striking midnight.

28
00:02:14.609 --> 00:02:15.890
I feel sleepy after all.

29
00:02:18.251 --> 00:02:18.991
Goodnight, Granny.

30
00:02:19.231 --> 00:02:20.112
I love you dearly.

31
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:30.458
Your granddaughter, Judy March 26 Dear Sir: You never answer any questions.

32
00:02:31.378 --> 00:02:34.380
You never show the slightest interest in anything I do.

33
00:02:35.616 --> 00:02:39.417
You are the most horrible of all the horrible trustees at the orphanage.

34
00:02:41.038 --> 00:02:43.738
You're only educating me out of a sense of duty.

35
00:02:44.919 --> 00:02:46.539
You don't care about me at all!

36
00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.720
I don't know a single thing about you.

37
00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.121
I don't even know your name.

38
00:02:55.421 --> 00:02:57.822
It's very boring to write to a thing.

39
00:02:58.742 --> 00:03:00.383
I doubt you even read my letters.

40
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:04.724
I'm sure you toss them into the trash without opening them.

41
00:03:06.276 --> 00:03:09.457
From now on, I will write only about my schoolwork.

42
00:03:10.737 --> 00:03:12.978
I retook my Latin and geometry exams.

43
00:03:13.898 --> 00:03:14.858
I passed them both.

44
00:03:16.619 --> 00:03:26.362
Yours truly, Jerusha Abbott April 2 Dear Daddy Longlegs, I am a BEAST.

45
00:03:27.302 --> 00:03:30.063
Please forget that horrible letter I sent last week.

46
00:03:31.323 --> 00:03:34.124
I was feeling lonely and miserable when I wrote.

47
00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:36.857
Plus, I had a sore throat.

48
00:03:40.039 --> 00:03:43.342
I didn't know it, but I was coming down with tonsillitis and the flu.

49
00:03:46.264 --> 00:03:47.445
I'm in the infirmary now.

50
00:03:48.946 --> 00:03:50.687
I've been here for six days!

51
00:03:52.748 --> 00:03:55.811
This is the first time they let me sit up and have pen and paper.

52
00:03:55.831 --> 00:03:58.753
(The head nurse is very bossy!)

53
00:04:00.274 --> 00:04:03.076
I've been thinking about that awful letter the whole time.

54
00:04:04.284 --> 00:04:06.125
I won't get well until you forgive me.

55
00:04:07.605 --> 00:04:08.845
I can't write anything more.

56
00:04:08.865 --> 00:04:16.067
I feel rather shaky; I think I've been sitting up too long.

57
00:04:17.328 --> 00:04:19.808
Please forgive me for being rude and ungrateful.

58
00:04:21.189 --> 00:04:22.289
I was badly brought up.

59
00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:35.037
Yours with love, Judy April 4 Dearest Daddy Longlegs, I am still in the infirmary.

60
00:04:36.679 --> 00:04:39.481
Yesterday afternoon I was sitting in bed, looking at the rain.

61
00:04:40.882 --> 00:04:43.704
I was feeling bored with life in this great institution.

62
00:04:44.824 --> 00:04:47.486
Suddenly a nurse appeared with a long white box.

63
00:04:49.027 --> 00:04:49.588
"For me?"

64
00:04:50.128 --> 00:04:51.089
I said in surprise.

65
00:04:51.109 --> 00:04:53.931
"What do you think is in inside?"

66
00:04:55.372 --> 00:04:56.193
The nurse laughed.

67
00:04:56.213 --> 00:05:00.576
(She was obviously a nice nurse, not the bossy and mean head nurse.)

68
00:05:01.864 --> 00:05:04.185
"You must have an admirer," she said.

69
00:05:04.205 --> 00:05:10.326
"There's usually only one thing that comes in a box like that—" "Roses!"

70
00:05:10.887 --> 00:05:12.767
I exclaimed as I lifted the cover.

71
00:05:14.248 --> 00:05:17.388
The box was filled with the loveliest pink roses!

72
00:05:18.609 --> 00:05:21.030
Thank you a thousand times, Daddy Longlegs.

73
00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.351
Your flowers are the first real present I've ever received.

74
00:05:27.691 --> 00:05:29.412
I know you sent me money for Christmas.

75
00:05:30.776 --> 00:05:33.678
But the roses prove that you were really thinking about me.

76
00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:37.720
And the card is even nicer than the roses.

77
00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.962
I can tell you wrote it yourself and didn't have your secretary do it.

78
00:05:43.003 --> 00:05:45.644
I thought the funny handwriting showed lots of personality.

79
00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:48.706
Do you want to know what a baby I am?

80
00:05:50.327 --> 00:05:53.388
I lay down and cried because I was so happy.

81
00:05:54.309 --> 00:05:56.150
I'm sure now that you read my letters.

82
00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.032
So I'll make them much more interesting.

83
00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:04.437
I hope you'll keep them tied with a red ribbon and locked in a safe.

84
00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:08.158
But please remove that rude letter and burn it.

85
00:06:09.158 --> 00:06:11.059
I hate to think that you ever read it.

86
00:06:12.279 --> 00:06:16.180
Thank you for thinking of a sick, miserable, and grumpy freshman.

87
00:06:16.961 --> 00:06:18.321
You made me very happy.

88
00:06:19.661 --> 00:06:22.062
You probably have lots of loving family and friends.

89
00:06:23.663 --> 00:06:25.523
So you don't know what it's like to feel alone.

90
00:06:26.143 --> 00:06:26.663
But I do.

91
00:06:27.604 --> 00:06:34.435
Good-bye. I promise never to be rude again because now I know you're a real person.

92
00:06:36.276 --> 00:06:39.197
I also promise never to bother you with any more questions.

93
00:06:40.038 --> 00:06:44.000
Yours forever, Judy P.S.

94
00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.942
Maybe I'll ask just one more question.

95
00:06:48.643 --> 00:06:49.843
Do you still hate girls?
